NAME
     httpd - a web server

SYNOPSIS
     httpd [-p PORT] [-d DIRECTORY] [-n]

DESCRIPTION
     httpd serves files under a directory over HTTP. It is started at
     boot by /etc/init.d/httpd and reads its settings from
     /etc/default/httpd.

OPTIONS
     -p PORT       listen there (80 by default)
     -d DIRECTORY  serve this directory (/srv/www by default)
     -n            stay in the foreground

SEE ALSO
     curl(1), service(8), netstat(1)
